{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CLS", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-uniqueness-and-diagonal}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d698940eb471e8266426b3ed21426a9cbad646703b1331ab59ad2c65faba459", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe result is Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe first state and prove a formal helper lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:30a840bb551c61040959276772bda71f29175733c8a729968357d8b209093c57", "unit_id": "tag:0CLS:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CLS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[rr]_-x \\ar[d]_j & &\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^{\\Delta_f} \\\\\n\\Spec(A) \\ar[rr]^{(a_1, a_2, \\varphi)} \\ar@{..>}[rru] & &\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$K$", "MATH_0006": "$\\gamma : (a_1, a_2, \\varphi) \\circ j \\longrightarrow \\Delta_f \\circ x$", "MATH_0007": "$2$", "MATH_0008": "$2$", "MATH_0009": "$\\gamma = (\\alpha_1, \\alpha_2)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\alpha_i : a_i \\circ j \\to x$", "MATH_0011": "$(a_1, \\alpha_1, \\text{id})$", "MATH_0012": "$(a_2, \\alpha_2, \\varphi)$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r]_-x \\ar[d]_j & \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n\\Spec(A) \\ar[r]^-{f \\circ a_1} \\ar@{..>}[ru] & \\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$\\gamma$", "MATH_0015": "$(a_1, \\alpha_1, \\text{id}) \\to (a_2, \\alpha_2, \\varphi)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-helper-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ad6e754ac021e38f80416f653ca507396782adb0ad394ff121e4aef040a6c7a7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:89d2513aa9fcbed0595e431092e82384cca560951b2252c3f0c82adb2ad178a8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nConsider a <MATH_0002>-commutative solid diagram\n<MATH_0003>\nwhere <MATH_0004> is a valuation ring with field of fractions <MATH_0005>. Let\n<MATH_0006>\nbe a <MATH_0007>-morphism witnessing the <MATH_0008>-commutativity of the diagram.\nThen\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Writing <MATH_0009> with\n<MATH_0010> we obtain two dotted arrows\n<MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012> in\nthe diagram\n<MATH_0013>\n<STRUCT_0003> The category of dotted arrows for the original diagram\nand <MATH_0014> is a setoid whose set of isomorphism\nclasses of objects equal to the set of morphisms\n<MATH_0015> in\nthe category of dotted arrows.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5dd74b9107523eb9046c2aac1abf795f83e779cc600562cc5e0142f31116499d", "unit_id": "tag:0E8L:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CLS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_f$", "MATH_0003": "$2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-cat-dotted-arrows}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e4e6e570b01c504c3ee0269b44527a4629f476f680d60f26cb15ecb889ea84af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cc345f1fe6fdaa4df21841268d94725e652af006ed56a1b7d6d7fdd994159efd", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001> is representable by algebraic spaces (hence the diagonal\nof <MATH_0002> is separated), we see that the category of dotted arrows\nin the first commutative diagram of the lemma is a setoid by\nLemma <REF_0001>. All the other statements\nof the lemma are consequences of <MATH_0003>-diagramatic\ncomputations which we omit.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:797dd611f80a3fa545343cd80280593403a1ada575ee5fbe1cac58f272cb01dc", "unit_id": "tag:0E8L:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CLS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-uniqueness-and-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f4b74bd44c9002222d6561aaadc5856f82b44c89e5bc1b5a7d413afc90d85fe9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4ce8ce82973ed4868e3c2691dc41439c1e27ec98d91a3523361cc9c97423fd01", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nAssume <MATH_0002> is quasi-separated.\nIf <MATH_0003> satisfies the uniqueness part of the valuative criterion,\nthen <MATH_0004> is separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6e22e0d5a3775932b347f36c3b0d5479e82a51bb8c32ce3e94f22f1000011992", "unit_id": "tag:0CLT:statement"}
